{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-luk-23-1","title":"Luke 23:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Jesus is accused before Pilate, and sent to Herod. 8 Herod mocks him. 12 Herod and Pilate are made friends. 13 Barabbas is desired of the people, and is loosed by Pilate, and Jesus is given to be crucified. 26 He tells the women, that lament him, the destruction of Jerusalem; 34 prays for his enemies. 39 Two evildoers are crucified with him. 46 His death. 50 His burial.</p>\n<p>22:66; Mt 27:1,2,11-14; Mr 15:1-5; Joh 18:28-38</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-2","title":"Luke 23:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>they. Zec 11:8; Mr 15:3-5; Joh 18:30 perverting. 5; 1Ki 18:17; Jer 38:4; Am 7:10; Ac 16:20,21; 17:6,7; 24:5 forbidding. 20:20-25; 1Ki 21:10-13; Ps 35:11; 62:4; 64:3-6; Jer 20:10; 37:13-15 Mt 17:27; 22:21; 26:59,60; Mr 12:17; 14:55,56; Ac 24:13; 1Pe 3:16-18 that. 22:69,70; Mr 14:61,62; Joh 18:36; 19:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-3","title":"Luke 23:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Pilate. Mt 27:11; Mr 15:2; Joh 18:33-37; 1Ti 6:13 the King. 38; 1:32,33; 19:38-40; Mr 15:18,32; Joh 1:49; 19:3,19-21 he answered. 1Ti 6:13 Thou sayest it.This was the most solemn mode of affirmation used by the Jews. When the inhabitants of Zippor, inquired whether Rabbi Judah were dead, the son of Kaphra answered, [atun amritun,] Ye say.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-4","title":"Luke 23:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>I find. 14,15; Mt 27:19,24; Mr 15:14; Joh 18:38; 19:4-6; Heb 7:26; 1Pe 1:19 1Pe 2:22; 3:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-5","title":"Luke 23:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>they. 23; 11:53; Ps 22:12,13,16; 57:4; 69:4; Mt 27:24; Joh 19:15; Ac 5:33 Ac 7:54,57; 23:10 beginning. 4:14,15; Mt 4:12-16,23; Mr 1:14; Joh 1:43; 2:11; 7:41,52; Ac 10:37</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-6","title":"Luke 23:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>a Galilean. 13:1; Ac 5:37</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-7","title":"Luke 23:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>Herod's. 3:1; 13:31</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-8","title":"Luke 23:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>for. 9:7-9; Mt 14:1; Mr 6:14 and he. 4:23; 2Ki 5:3-6,11; Ac 8:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-9","title":"Luke 23:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>but. 13:32; Ps 38:13,14; 39:1,2,9; Isa 53:7; Mt 7:6; 27:14; Ac 8:32 1Pe 2:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-10","title":"Luke 23:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>and vehemently. 2,5,14,15; 11:53; Ac 24:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-11","title":"Luke 23:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>Herod. Ac 4:27,28 set. 22:64,65; Ps 22:6; 69:19,20; Isa 49:7; 53:3; Mt 27:27-30; Mr 9:12 Mr 15:16-20 arrayed. Joh 19:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-12","title":"Luke 23:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>Ps 83:4-6; Ac 4:27; Mt 16:1; Re 17:13,14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-13","title":"Luke 23:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Mt 27:21-23; Mr 15:14; Joh 18:38; 19:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-14","title":"Luke 23:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>as one. 1,2,5 have found. 4; Da 6:4; Mt 27:4,19,24,54; Ac 13:28; Heb 7:26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-15","title":"Luke 23:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>nothing.Rather, \"nothing worthy of death is committed my him;\" [prasso autou ] being put for [hupo autou ,] or [prasso autos ,] \"he hath done nothing.\"</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-16","title":"Luke 23:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>Isa 53:5; Mt 27:26; Mr 15:15; Joh 19:1-4; Ac 5:40,41</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-17","title":"Luke 23:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>Mt 27:15; Mr 15:6; Joh 18:39</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-18","title":"Luke 23:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>they. Mt 27:16-23; Mr 15:7-14; Joh 18:40; Ac 3:14 Away. Joh 19:15; Ac 21:36; 22:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-19","title":"Luke 23:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>2,5; Ac 3:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-20","title":"Luke 23:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>Mt 14:8,9; 27:19; Mr 15:15; Joh 19:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-21","title":"Luke 23:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>23; Mt 27:22-25; Mr 15:13; Joh 19:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-22","title":"Luke 23:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>Why. 14,20; 1Pe 1:19; 3:18 I will. 16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-23","title":"Luke 23:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>5; Ps 22:12,13; 57:4; Zec 11:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-24","title":"Luke 23:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>Pilate. Mt 27:26; Mr 15:15; Joh 19:1 gave sentence. or, assented. Ex 23:2; Pr 17:15 it. Ex 23:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-25","title":"Luke 23:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>for. 2,5; Mr 15:7; Joh 18:40 whom. 1Sa 12:13; Mr 15:6; Ac 3:14 but. Mt 27:26; Mr 15:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-26","title":"Luke 23:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>they laid. Mt 27:32-44; Mr 15:21-32; Joh 19:16 a Cyrenian. Ac 2:10; 6:6,9; 13:1 that. 9:23; 14:27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-27","title":"Luke 23:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>and of. 55; 8:2; Mt 27:55; Mr 15:40</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-28","title":"Luke 23:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>daughters. So 1:5; 2:7; 3:5,10; 5:8,16; 8:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-29","title":"Luke 23:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>the days.Our Lord here refers to the destruction of Jerusalem, and the final desolation of the Jewish state; an evil associated with so many miseries, that sterility, which had otherwise been considered an opprobrium, was accounted a circumstance most felicitous. No history can furnish us with a parallel to the calamities and miseries of the Jews; rapine and murder, famine and pestilence, within; fire and sword, and all the terrors of war, without. Our Saviour himself wept at the foresight of these calamities; and it is almost impossible for persons of any humanity to read the relation of them in Josephus without weeping also. He might justly affirm, \"if the misfortunes of all, from the beginning of the world, were compared with those of the Jews, they would appear much inferior in the comparison.\"</p>\n<p>21:23,24; Mt 24:19; Mr 13:17-19 Blessed. De 28:53-57; Ho 9:12-16; 13:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-30","title":"Luke 23:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>Isa 2:19; Ho 10:8; Re 6:16; 9:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-31","title":"Luke 23:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>Pr 11:31; Jer 25:29; Eze 15:2-7; 20:47,48; 21:3,4; Da 9:26; Mt 3:12 Joh 15:6; Heb 6:8; 1Pe 4:17,18; Jude 1:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-32","title":"Luke 23:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>22:37; Isa 53:12; Mt 27:38; Mr 15:27,28; Joh 19:18; Heb 12:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-33","title":"Luke 23:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>when. Mt 27:33,34; Mr 15:22,23; Joh 19:17,18; Heb 13:12,13 Calvary. or, the place of a skull. they crucified. 24:7; De 21:23; Ps 22:16; Zec 12:10; Mt 20:19; 26:2; Mr 10:33,34 Joh 3:14; 12:33,34; 18:32; Ac 2:23; 5:30; 13:29; Ga 3:13; 1Pe 2:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-34","title":"Luke 23:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>Father. 47,48; 6:27,28; Ge 50:17; Ps 106:16-23; Mt 5:44; Ac 7:60; Ro 12:14 1Co 4:12; 1Pe 2:20-23; 3:9 they know not. 12:47,48; Joh 15:22-24; 19:11; Ac 3:17; 1Co 2:8; 1Ti 1:13 And they. Ps 22:18; Mt 27:35,36; Mr 15:24; Joh 19:23,24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-35","title":"Luke 23:35","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":35,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":35},"content":"<p>the people. Ps 22:12,13,17; Zec 12:10; Mt 27:38-43; Mr 15:29-32 derided. 16:14; Ge 37:19,20; Ps 4:2; 35:15,19-25; 69:7-12,26; 71:11; Isa 49:7 Isa 53:3; La 3:14 Christ. 22:67-70; Ps 22:6-8; Isa 42:1; Mt 3:17; 12:18; 1Pe 2:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-36","title":"Luke 23:36","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":36,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":36},"content":"<p>11; Ps 69:21; Mt 27:29,30,34,48; Mr 15:19,20,36; Joh 19:28-30</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-38","title":"Luke 23:38","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":38,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":38},"content":"<p>3; Mt 27:11,37; Mr 15:18,26,32; Joh 19:3,19-22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-39","title":"Luke 23:39","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":39,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":39},"content":"<p>17:34-36; Mt 27:44; Mr 15:32</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-40","title":"Luke 23:40","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":40,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":40},"content":"<p>rebuked. Le 19:17; Eph 5:11 Dost. 12:5; Ps 36:1; Re 15:4 seeing. 2Ch 28:22; Jer 5:3; Re 16:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-41","title":"Luke 23:41","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":41,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":41},"content":"<p>we indeed. 15:18,19; Le 26:40,41; Jos 7:19,20; 2Ch 33:12; Ezr 9:13; Ne 9:3 Da 9:4; Jas 4:7; 1Jo 1:8,9 but. 41; 22:69,70; Mt 27:4,19,24,54; 1Pe 1:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-42","title":"Luke 23:42","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":42,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":42},"content":"<p>Lord. 18:13; Ps 106:4,5; Joh 20:28; Ac 16:31; 20:21; Ro 10:9-14 1Co 6:10,11; 1Pe 2:6,7; 1Jo 5:1,11-13 when. 12:8; Joh 1:49; Ro 10:9,10 thy. 24:26; Ps 2:6; Isa 9:6,7; 53:10-12; Da 7:13,14; 1Pe 1:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-43","title":"Luke 23:43","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":43,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":43},"content":"<p>To day. 15:4,5,20-24; 19:10; Job 33:27-30; Ps 32:5; 50:15; Isa 1:18,19 Isa 53:11; 55:6-9; 65:24; Mic 7:18; Mt 20:15,16; Ro 5:20,21 1Ti 1:15,16; Heb 7:25 with. Joh 14:3; 17:24; 2Co 5:8; Php 1:23 in. 2Co 12:4; Re 2:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-44","title":"Luke 23:44","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":44,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":44},"content":"<p>it. Mt 27:45; Mr 15:33 there. Ex 10:21-23; Ps 105:28; Joe 2:31; Am 5:18; 8:9; Hab 3:8-11; Ac 2:20 earth. or, land.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-45","title":"Luke 23:45","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":45,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":45},"content":"<p>and the veil. Ex 26:31; Le 16:12-16; 2Ch 3:14; Mt 27:51; Mr 15:38; Eph 2:14-18 Heb 6:19; 9:3-8; 10:19-22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23-46","title":"Luke 23:46","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":46,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":46},"content":"<p>cried. Mt 27:46-49; Mr 15:34-36 Father. Ps 31:5; Ac 7:59; 1Pe 2:23 having. Mt 27:50-56; Mr 15:37-41; Joh 19:30</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-23